        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: கிருமி",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கிருமி — kirumi — \"a germ; a microbe\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கை கழுவினால் கிருமிகள் போகும். kai kaḻuviṉāl kirumikaḷ pōkum. If you wash your hands, the germs go away."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: கிருமிகள், kirumikaḷ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its plural is regular: கிருமிகள்."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கிருமி (kirumi) is borrowed from Sanskrit kṛmi, \"a worm, an insect\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
